No codebase in the working dir, so this is framework-agnostic; `/api/search` and `render` are placeholders.

```js
const input = document.querySelector('#search');
let timer, controller;

input.addEventListener('input', () => {
  clearTimeout(timer);
  timer = setTimeout(async () => {
    controller?.abort();
    controller = new AbortController();
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(input.value)}`, { signal: controller.signal });
      render(await res.json());
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.name !== 'AbortError') throw e;
    }
  }, 300);
});
```

React equivalent:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timer = setTimeout(() => {
    fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`, { signal: controller.signal })
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(setResults)
      .catch(e => { if (e.name !== 'AbortError') throw e; });
  }, 300);
  return () => { clearTimeout(timer); controller.abort(); };
}, [query]);
```

Debounce alone still lets a slow early response land after a newer one → stale results; `AbortController` cancels the in-flight request. 300ms is a common default; drop to 150–200 if it feels laggy.

